	(text "Board-wide output edge selection"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 133.858 18.034 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "debc934d-728a-4862-b288-3bc5c86bd06c")
	)
	(text_box "The clock signal provided on the connector may not be able to drive all 8 microphones. This clock buffer has low additive jitter (<28 fs, depending on supply voltage), a propagation delay < 3ns, and < 55ps output-to-output skew. Output impedance is 50 ohms, so we do not need termination resistors if we make the characteristic impedance of the trace 50 ohms."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 119.38 0)
		(size 54.61 16.51)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1bc020cd-f09e-40b2-9c35-5eff1ceafc01")
	)
	(text_box "The microphone PDM signals can be configured to output on either the rising or falling edge of the clock. Two complementary outputs can be multiplexed on one line. Short these jumpers to perform this multiplexing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 68.58 0)
		(size 54.61 11.43)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4171693f-73e1-4b6d-ba9c-83f3cc6604da")
	)
	(text_box "Each microphone has a solder bridge (JP0 through JP7) to configure its select (SEL) line. One of those options is the board-wide level set by JP8. This can be set to Vdd, ground, or the voltage on the connector."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 21.59 0)
		(size 54.61 11.43)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8532c780-dbdb-48b5-b88b-3abe187e3bc5")
	)
	(text_box "MEMS microphones with pulse density modulation (PDM) outputs. If select (SEL) is connected to Vdd, the output is driven after a rising clock edge and held until after the next falling edge (i.e., read it on the falling edge). If SEL is grounded, the opposite is true. This is configured by solder jumpers; BSEL corresponds to a board-wide value (JP8). The outputs are in a high-impedance state when not driven.\n\nThe datasheet recommends avoiding class 2 dielectrics for capacitors close to the microphones as these can have a piezoelectric effect.\n\nSource termination resistors for the PDM line are included; populate these with something other than 0 ohms if desired."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 20.32 0)
		(size 105.41 21.59)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a0212b2d-5dc7-4ccc-bca2-53163432f7fc")
	)
	(text_box "Pick an LED colour with a forward voltage drop lower than the set Vdd, then set the resistor to give the desired current. 330 ohms gives a 4mA current with a 3.3V Vdd and an orange LED with 2V forward drop."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 124.46 0)
		(size 54.61 8.89)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b05a16cf-144e-4581-b1cd-d639f331ed05")
	)
	(text_box "2 x M3 mounting holes. Electrically isolated, but with a number of vias within the pad for extra strength against crushing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 172.72 0)
		(size 54.61 7.62)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c836be14-234d-455d-8180-8e66feef2559")
	)
	(text_box "1.8V: MAX8891EXK18+T   2.5V: MAX8891EXK25+T \n3.3V: MAX8891EXK33+T\n\nThe dropout voltage is ~50mV at the expected 40mA so this can still be used if Vin is the same as the desired Vdd. Alternatively, do not place U1 and short JP13."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 68.58 0)
		(size 54.61 15.24)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dd9c376f-093b-448a-b32e-763949728e41")
	)
	(text_box "If the microphone outputs are multiplexed to four lines (JP9 through JP12 shorted), then an 8 pin connector (corresponding to pins 1-8 of the 12 pin connector) can be used."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 21.59 0)
		(size 54.61 10.082)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
